BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Stanford Law] Reimagining American Institutions
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20270115T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20270115T170000
DTSTAMP:20261124T225803Z
UID:stanford_campus-law-10003612-1800000000-1800032400@law.stanford.edu-20
 27-01-15T08:00:00-08:00@local-events
DESCRIPTION:In the cacophony of discourse in the United States\, virtually
  everyone agrees on at least this: our institutions are failing to transla
 te the will of the people into collective action that addresses the major 
 challenges of this century. The purpose of this conference is to address t
 hree critical problem areas — the rule of law\, the environment\, and ar
 tificial intelligence — by reimagining the structure and function of ins
 titutions dedicated to achieving pragmatic solutions in a democratic way.
 \n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://law.stanford.edu/event/reimagining-ame
 rican-institutions/\nLast synced: 2026-11-24 14:58 PST
LOCATION:@ Stanford: Paul Brest Hall\, 555 Salvatierra Walk\, Stanford\, C
 A\, 94305\, United States
URL:https://law.stanford.edu/event/reimagining-american-institutions/
END:VEVENT
